--[[
Task Manager: what is running on the computer and how hard it is
working, as a Mac's Activity Monitor shows it.

  saule run .

    model   what is running (Monitor), read from `saule-tasks`, and what
            the window is showing of it (Listing)
    views   the window: an overview of the processor, memory and
            graphics; the apps that are open; every process; and the
            services started with the system

The figures come from `saule-tasks` (saule-linux's `system/src/tasks.rs`),
which the app starts and reads a sample from every other second. Where
that program is missing, on another system, the window says so.
]]

from TaskManagerApp import TaskManagerApp

class Main
  static fn main()
    TaskManagerApp().run()
  end
end
